Description: Bangla Lekhi — Native Bengali phonetic input method for Linux
 Bangla Lekhi is a native IBus input method engine for typing Bengali
 (Bangla) using Avro-compatible phonetic transliteration on Linux.
 .
 Features:
  - Avro-compatible phonetic typing (system-wide: GTK, Qt, browsers)
  - Instant candidate suggestions via upodesh FST dictionary
  - Configurable toggle key (default F12; Ctrl+Space supported)
  - User custom word dictionary
  - Clipboard history sourced from the system clipboard
  - GTK4/Libadwaita settings application
  - Lightweight Rust+C engine (~3 MB RAM usage)
  - GPL-3.0-or-later licensed, 100% offline, no telemetry
